-- title:
--   Constant for the endpoint error pairing
-- statement:
--   The error pairing constant is the product
--   $$
--   C_{\mathrm{err}}=K_{\mathrm{env}}\cdot C_{\mathrm{mesh}}\cdot C_{\mathrm{jump}}>0,
--   $$
--   where $K_{\mathrm{env}}$ is the envelope constant with $|\mathrm{errorProfile}(v)|\le K_{\mathrm{env}}|v|\phi_6(v)$, $C_{\mathrm{mesh}}=2e^{1/2}$ bounds Gaussian Riemann sums, and $C_{\mathrm{jump}}=2+48\sqrt2$ bounds single-entry energy jumps.
--
--   It bounds the contribution of the endpoint errors, the difference between smooth and sharp truncations, to the cyclic pairing.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/ErrorPairing.lean

